Job Description for L9: 
  
A Test Data Management (TDM)  Engineer/Analyst with expertise in Data Provisioning, Maintaining Referential Integrity, Data Refreshing & Versioning and Gold Copy creation. 
  
Responsibilities: 
  
Experience in defining and implement enterprise Test Data Management strategy. 
Lead TDM activities across multiple applications, projects, and testing environments. 
Analyze application data requirements and identify appropriate test-data sets. 
Design processes for test-data creation, extraction, masking, Subsetting, cloning, refresh, and provisioning. 
Ensure sensitive data such as PII, PHI, and PCI is appropriately masked or anonymized. 
Develop reusable and automated test-data provisioning solutions. 
Integrate TDM processes with CI/CD and automated testing frameworks. 
Work closely with QA, development, DBA, DevOps, security, architecture, and business teams. 
Establish TDM governance, standards, processes, and KPIs. 
Manage test-data refreshes from source environments. 
Optimize test-data provisioning time and infrastructure costs. 
Evaluate and implement TDM tools and technologies. 
Troubleshoot data-quality, dependency, provisioning, and environment issues. 
Mentor TDM engineers and establish best practices. 
Ensure compliance with organizational data-security and privacy policies. 
  
